menu "DS18B20 / 1-Wire"

    config ONEWIRE_INTERNAL_PULLUP
        bool "Enable the internal pull-up on the 1-Wire pins"
        default n
        help
            The 1-Wire bus needs a pull-up resistor (4.7 kOhm to the MCU logic level, DS18B20
            datasheet). The internal one (~45 kOhm on ESP32 chips) is enough only for short wires
            and a development setup; with long sensor cables use the external resistor.

    config DS18B20_POLL_CONVERSION
        bool "Poll the end of the conversion (externally powered sensors)"
        default y
        help
            An externally powered DS18B20 answers read time slots with 0 while converting and 1
            when done (datasheet), so a measurement takes as long as the conversion really does
            (typically less than 750 ms). Turn it off for sensors that do not support this
            (some clones): the driver then always waits 750 ms. Parasite powered sensors always
            get the full 750 ms with the strong pull-up.

endmenu
